spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:35:- **Ordered Queue**: A CLI-provided sequence of issue identifiers used as the dispatch order for eligible work.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:44:- **REQ-003**: One Stage Agent that owns multiple statuses MUST share one concurrency limit across all owned statuses.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:46:- **REQ-005**: Symphony MUST NOT exceed either a Stage Agent concurrency limit or the global concurrency cap.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:47:- **REQ-006**: Omitted per-stage concurrency MUST preserve current behavior for that Stage Agent.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:51:- **REQ-010**: Symphony MUST NOT pre-spawn idle agents.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:54:- **REQ-013**: Ordered Queue admission order MUST remain authoritative for queued work.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:56:- **REQ-015**: Running, retrying, blocked, and Human Attention tasks MUST NOT be double-dispatched.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:57:- **REQ-016**: Runtime State SHOULD expose enough data to explain per-stage running counts and blocked capacity.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:58:- **CON-001**: This Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository SHOULD keep practical concurrency at one until safe parallel Task Branch Integration is implemented.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:105:| Ordered Queue has eligible entry but stage cap is full | Keep entry pending until capacity exists. |
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:112:- **AC-004**: Given an Ordered Queue, When the next queued issue has stage capacity, Then it is admitted according to queue order.
spec/spec-process-stage-concurrency-policy.md:113:- **AC-005**: Given an Ordered Queue entry is otherwise eligible but its Stage Agent is at capacity, When a later queue entry has different stage capacity, Then queue semantics determine whether the later entry may be admitted.
