docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:9:It is written as a planning artifact for Personal Symphony. It does not change the Runtime Contract yet. Any implementation that introduces new Runtime Settings, Runtime State files, or domain language should update `CONTEXT.md` and add an ADR under `docs/adr/`.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:13:`codex-loop` does not implement full transcript compression in its harness. It keeps compact loop state in local JSON, then uses Codex lifecycle hooks to inject a new continuation prompt when Codex stops too early.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:23:Activation is explicit. A loop starts only when the first user prompt line contains a `[[CODEX_LOOP ...]]` header. The `UserPromptSubmit` hook parses that header, resolves a workspace root, supersedes older active loops for the same Codex `session_id`, and writes a `LoopRecord` under `${CODEX_HOME}/codex-loop/loops/`.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:27:Continuation happens through the `Stop` hook. When Codex stops, the hook resolves the active loop by `session_id`, updates `last_assistant_message` and counters, checks the limiter, and either marks the loop complete or returns hook JSON with `decision: "block"` and a generated `reason`. Codex treats that reason as the next continuation instruction.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:29:`pre_loop_continue` is a synchronous harness-side context hook. It runs only after `codex-loop` has already decided to continue. The command receives structured JSON on stdin and through env vars, stdout is appended to the next continuation prompt, stderr is discarded, failures become short warnings, and output is capped by `max_output_bytes`.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:33:Observability is deliberately small. Goal attempts append metadata to `${CODEX_HOME}/codex-loop/runs.jsonl`, but the README states that full task prompts, assistant messages, confirmation prompts, reviewer text, interpreter prompts, and `pre_loop_continue` output are not stored in that log.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:39:- Local JSON state: `${CODEX_HOME}/codex-loop/loops/*.json` and `${CODEX_HOME}/codex-loop/runs.jsonl`.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:40:- Runtime TOML config: global `${CODEX_HOME}/codex-loop/config.toml` plus nearest project `codex-loop.toml`.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:63:- goal interpretation: convert reviewer prose into schema-valid verdict JSON.
docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md:74:- `internal/loop/pre_loop_continue.go:121-188`: structured JSON input, env values, timeout, stdout capture, and stderr discard.
