+99:**Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy**:
+100:A Runtime Settings rule that identifies which Loop-Start Branches may dispatch automated orchestration.
+104:A repository-owned rule that identifies Workspace Repository paths agent work must not modify without explicit authorization.
+112:The `prompt.md` portion of the Runtime Contract that defines the task instructions rendered for each dispatched issue.
+128:The ignored files inside the Runtime Home that record current orchestration activity and recovery data.
+132:Ignored Runtime Home metadata that helps explain orchestration behavior without changing the Runtime Contract.
+152:An optional push of a Stage Commit to the currently checked-out Task Branch after the Stage Commit is created.
+184:A single pull request opened from the Loop-Start Branch either after Symphony reaches Orchestration Idle or, when configured, after task work moves to the review status.
