+192:An optional non-force push of the Loop-Start Branch before opening a Batch Pull Request.
+220:A Loop-Start Branch checkout with no uncommitted Workspace Repository changes.
+224:The startup-time recovery pass that checks completed-stage Agent Worktrees for Task Branch commits not present on the Loop-Start Branch.
+227:**Task Branch Integration**:
+228:The serialized act of bringing completed Task Branch commits into the Loop-Start Branch, directly by fast-forward when possible or by first updating the Task Branch from the current Loop-Start Branch.
+232:The default terminal interface for operating Personal Symphony in a Workspace Repository.
+236:The optional browser interface for operating Personal Symphony in a Workspace Repository.
+284:A Bootstrap that creates missing Runtime Home files without overwriting user-edited files.
+289:- A **Workspace Repository** may receive a **Bootstrap** from Personal Symphony.
+290:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** is both a **Product Repository** and a **Workspace Repository**.
+291:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may commit a real **Runtime Contract** for its own Personal Symphony runs.
+292:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use a dedicated GitHub Project as its dispatch board.
+293:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may enable **Stage Goal Handoff** on every configured **Stage Agent**.
+294:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may use its planner stage as a PRD review gate for already-refined issues.
+295:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use **Stage Commit** to create local engineer-stage commits before review.
+296:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should keep **Stage Push** disabled unless remote branch publication is deliberately enabled.
+297:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use reviewer-stage comments and a **Human Attention Status** for review findings that require operator triage.
+298:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should have the reviewer stage run focused verification when practical before moving work to `Done`.
+299:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may increase concurrency when its **Loop-Start Branch** is not a **Protected Trunk Branch** because **Task Branch Integration** can integrate unrelated concurrently completed **Task Branches**.
+300:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should use a dedicated non-trunk **Loop-Start Branch** so completed **Task Branches** do not auto-merge into the Product Repository trunk.
+301:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** may open a **Batch Pull Request** from its dedicated **Loop-Start Branch** to its **Protected Trunk Branch** after **Orchestration Idle**.
+302:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should remove merged **Agent Worktrees** and delete merged **Task Branches** to avoid local branch buildup.
+303:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should prevent accidental dogfood dispatch from the Product Repository trunk.
+304:- A **Self-Dogfooding Workspace Repository** should define a **Protected Path Policy** for release and package files once that policy exists.
+305:- An **Idempotent Bootstrap** must preserve existing Runtime Contract and Local Environment files.
+306:- A **Workspace Repository** contains at most one **Runtime Home**.
+307:- Personal Symphony commands must be run from the root of a **Workspace Repository**.
+308:- Personal Symphony exits before Bootstrap when the current directory is not the root of a **Workspace Repository**.
+309:- A **Runtime Home** contains the **Runtime Contract**, user-editable settings, and internal state.
+310:- The **Runtime Contract** contains **Runtime Settings**.
+311:- The **Runtime Contract** contains an **Agent Prompt**.
+312:- A **Runtime Home** contains one **Environment Template** and may contain one **Local Environment**.
+313:- A **Runtime Home** may contain **Runtime State**.
+314:- A **Runtime Home** may contain many **Agent Workspaces**.
+320:- A **PI Harness** must preserve Agent Worktree, Task Branch, Agent Prompt, Stage Commit, Stage Push, retry, and status transition behavior.
+322:- A **Git Policy** may contain an **Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy**.
+323:- A **Workspace Repository** may define a **Protected Path Policy**.
+333:- Agent Worktrees live under the Runtime Home workspaces directory.
+334:- Each **Agent Worktree** checks out one **Task Branch**.
+335:- Each **Task Branch** starts from the **Loop-Start Branch**.
+336:- Each **Task Branch** name starts with the **Task Branch Prefix** and includes the task's stable issue number.
+337:- If a task enters work without an existing **Task Branch**, the **Task Branch** starts from the current **Loop-Start Branch**.
+338:- If a task already has a **Task Branch**, Symphony reuses it.
+342:- Symphony may auto-merge a completed **Task Branch** into the **Loop-Start Branch** only when the **Loop-Start Branch** is not a **Protected Trunk Branch**.
+343:- Auto-merge of a **Task Branch** into the **Loop-Start Branch** keeps the final **Loop-Start Branch** update fast-forward only.
+344:- If the **Loop-Start Branch** cannot fast-forward directly to a completed **Task Branch**, Symphony may update the **Task Branch** by merging the current **Loop-Start Branch** into it from the **Agent Worktree**, then fast-forward the **Loop-Start Branch** to the updated **Task Branch**.
+346:- Auto-merge, **Startup Reconciliation**, and **Manual Task Merge** are **Task Branch Integration** paths.
+347:- An **Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy** prevents dispatch from any Loop-Start Branch outside the configured literal branch set.
+348:- An omitted or empty **Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy** allows any Loop-Start Branch.
+349:- A disallowed **Loop-Start Branch** is a **Readiness Gap** that keeps the **Terminal Console** and **Web Dashboard** available for inspection while blocking dispatch, **Startup Reconciliation**, and **Batch Pull Request** creation.
+351:- **Manual Task Merge** accepts issue identifiers such as `20` and `#20`; it does not accept raw **Task Branch** names.
+357:- **Startup Reconciliation** uses the same safe **Task Branch Integration** path as normal completion.
+358:- **Startup Reconciliation** does not create a **Stage Commit**, reconcile retained **Task Branches** without **Agent Worktrees**, or change tracker status after successful or already-contained reconciliation.
+360:- **Runtime State** records **Task Branch Integration** diagnostics for direct fast-forwards, update-then-fast-forward integrations, already-contained branches, and integration attention.
+364:- The default **Task Cleanup Policy** removes an **Agent Worktree** after its **Task Branch** is merged.
+365:- The default **Task Cleanup Policy** keeps a merged **Task Branch**.
+370:- A **Workspace Repository** may define **Stage Commit Tag Guidance** in `tags.json`.
+379:- A **Stage Push** sends the **Stage Commit** to the currently checked-out **Task Branch**.
+383:- **Startup Reconciliation**, **Task Branch Integration**, and **Manual Task Merge** must refuse unauthorized protected path changes before integrating committed **Task Branch** work.
+385:- A **Stage Push** pushes the current **Task Branch** tip, including earlier unpushed commits on that branch.
+387:- A **Stage Push** uses the current **Task Branch** upstream when one exists.
+388:- A **Stage Push** creates an upstream on `origin` when the current **Task Branch** has no upstream.
+390:- **Task Branch Integration** must not force-push a **Task Branch** after **Stage Push**.
+391:- Symphony does not push the **Loop-Start Branch** after auto-merge.
+416:- Missing **Agent Context Snapshot** or **Context Command** settings preserve existing Runtime Contract behavior.
+446:- An **Ordered Queue** is named with issue identifiers from the Workspace Repository issue tracker.
+455:- An **Ordered Queue Entry** is invalid when it is malformed, missing from the Workspace Repository issue tracker, absent from the configured GitHub Project, terminal, or not dispatchable.
+459:- The **Runtime Home** state directory stores the active **Ordered Queue** Runtime State projection for ordinary process restart resume.
+475:- A **Batch Pull Request** represents the combined task work already integrated into the **Loop-Start Branch**.
+479:- A **Batch Pull Request** uses the **Loop-Start Branch** as its head branch.
+481:- Symphony reports a **Readiness Gap** when automatic **Batch Pull Request** creation is enabled and the current **Loop-Start Branch** is the same branch as the configured **Pull Request Base Branch**.
+484:- A **Task Pull Request** uses a completed task's **Task Branch** as its head branch.
+487:- Symphony may open **Task Pull Requests** while the current **Loop-Start Branch** is the same branch as the configured **Pull Request Base Branch**.
+488:- A **Task Pull Request** does not require **Task Branch Integration** into the **Loop-Start Branch** before handoff.
+489:- A **Task Pull Request** handoff pushes the **Task Branch** non-force before opening or reusing the pull request.
+499:- A **Batch Branch Push** pushes the **Loop-Start Branch** to its remote head branch.
+503:- The **Runtime Contract** is version-controlled with the Workspace Repository.
+551:- The **Product Repository** provides the **CLI Package**.
+555:- `symphony update` updates the installed **CLI Package** and does not require a **Workspace Repository**.
+556:- `symphony update` supports npm-installed **CLI Package** instances and does not update Product Repository source checkouts.
+566:> **Dev:** "When the user runs the CLI, should we write files into the **Product Repository**?"
+567:> **Domain expert:** "No, runtime files belong in the **Workspace Repository** where the user invoked Personal Symphony."
+571:> **Domain expert:** "Inside the **Runtime Home** as **Agent Workspaces**, and the bootstrap should add them to the Runtime Home gitignore."
+575:> **Domain expert:** "No, the **Runtime Contract** lives inside the **Runtime Home**."
+581:> **Domain expert:** "No, it pushes the currently checked-out **Task Branch**, because the agent may be running inside an **Agent Worktree**."
+582:> **Dev:** "What if the current **Task Branch** has no upstream yet?"
+613:- "project" was used to mean both the Personal Symphony source repository and the user's repository; resolved: use **Product Repository** for this repo and **Workspace Repository** for the repository where the CLI runs.
+617:- "push to the branch that we are in" was used to mean pushing the currently checked-out **Task Branch**, especially from an **Agent Worktree**.
+624:- "Open PR after finishing all the tasks" was used to mean opening one pull request for combined task work; resolved: use **Batch Pull Request**, opened from the **Loop-Start Branch** after **Orchestration Idle** by default.
+626:- "Start on main, but open PRs from each Task Branch into main" means using `task` **Pull Request Mode** to open **Task Pull Requests**.
+628:- "merge the worktrees" was used to mean integrating completed **Task Branches**; resolved: Symphony fast-forward merges **Task Branches** into the **Loop-Start Branch**, not Agent Worktrees.
+630:- "allowed branch" was used to mean restricting where orchestration may start; resolved: use **Allowed Loop-Start Branch Policy**.
 
